    <briefdescription>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>For rendering we need to store most of OpenGL&apos;s stuff such as the vertex array object, vertex buffer object &amp; the shader program as well as hooks and the zdepth level.</para>
<para>Additionally we represent draw calls with a linked list queue that points to the image and the index of its instance. Again, instances only carry XYZ data, so coupled with the image it lets us know where to draw a copy of the image.</para>
<para>Texture contexts are kept in a struct alongside the capacity of the array of instances, since the array is realloced like a vector. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
